    <!-- Watch Out For -->
    <section class="exam-section" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #fff3cd 0%, #ffe5a0 100%); border-left-color: #ffc107;">
        <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation section-icon" style="color: #856404;"></i> Common Misconceptions</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>More Data is Better:</strong> Believing all data is useful; students must understand that irrelevant features (noise) can degrade model performance.</li>
            <li><strong>Cleaning as a One-off:</strong> Viewing cleaning as the first step only, rather than an iterative process throughout model development.</li>
            <li><strong>Linearity:</strong> Assuming all relationships in nature are linear; identifying when Linear Regression is an inappropriate model.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

